WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.889
When the weather turns in the mountains,
don't push on until you are exhausted.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:07.611
The Norwegian mountain code says it plainly:

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.667
save your energy, and seek shelter if necessary.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:16.922
Look for a deep snowdrift on the sheltered side
of a ridge, well away from avalanche terrain.

00:00:17.144 --> 00:00:19.366
Check the depth with a ski pole or a probe.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:23.400
Dig a tunnel straight in,
about as wide and as tall as you are.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:28.845
Then dig upwards and to the sides, and shape sleeping
benches at least half a metre above the tunnel floor.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.512
Cold air is heavy.

00:00:30.623 --> 00:00:34.289
It sinks into the tunnel and stays there,
while you rest in the warmer air above.

00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:37.655
Keep the roof and walls
at least half a metre thick,

00:00:37.655 --> 00:00:40.877
and smooth the ceiling into an even dome,
so it does not drip.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:45.911
Push a ski pole through the roof
to make an air hole, and keep it open.

00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:49.356
Then close off the top of the entrance
with snow blocks.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.944
Bring the shovel inside.

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:55.611
Plant your skis upright outside,
so the cave can be found.

00:00:55.833 --> 00:01:00.055
A candle is your air gauge: if it starts
to burn poorly, let in more air.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.200
Outside, it may be twenty below.

00:01:03.255 --> 00:01:05.644
Inside, it stays close to freezing.

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:08.589
Practise this on a good day,
before you ever need it.

